    "title": "Bismark State College recognizes spring graduates, including two locals - NewsBreak",
    "text": "10 hours ago BISMARCK, N.D. – More than 650 students graduated with degrees from Bismarck State College after completing the spring 2026 semester, including two from southeast Wyoming.\nZachary McGee, of Cheyenne, graduated with a Certificate in Instrumentation and Control Technology, while Anthony Apodaca, of Wheatland, graduated with a Bachelor of Applied Science in Energy Management.\nThe graduates were recognized at the college's 86th commencement ceremony on May 15 at the BSC Bavendick Center.",
    "summary": "7 hours ago BISMARCK, N.D. – More than 650 students graduated with degrees from Bismarck State College after completing the spring 2026 semester, including two from southeast Wyoming. Zachary McGee, of Cheyenne, graduated with a Certificate in Instrumentation and Control Technology, while Anthony Apodaca, of Wheatland, graduated with a Bachelor of Applied Science in Energy Management. The graduates were recognized at the college's 86th commencement ceremony on May 15 at the BSC Bavendick Center.",
